      "title": "About — Larkmoor Press",
      "lang": "en",
      "canonicalUrl": null,
      "metaDescription": "How Larkmoor Press works, and where to find its books.",
      "outline": [
        {
          "tag": "header",
          "role": null,
          "level": null,
          "text": "About Larkmoor A two-person press working to a deliberately small calendar. Home About",
          "selector": "html > body > header"
        },
        {
          "tag": "h1",
          "role": null,
          "level": 1,
          "text": "About Larkmoor",
          "selector": "html > body > header > h1"
        },
        {
          "tag": "nav",
          "role": null,
          "level": null,
          "text": "Home About",
          "selector": "html > body > header > nav"
        },
        {
          "tag": "main",
          "role": null,
          "level": null,
          "text": "How we work Manuscripts arrive by post. We read them away from a screen, answer every one, and take on two a year. An accepted book is edited over eight months, set in metal for the title pages, and printed in runs of nine hundred. Nothing is reprinted. When a run is gone the book stays gone, which keeps the shelf honest and the workshop quiet. Where to find us Booksellers who stock Larkmoor, and the two markets we attend each year. Home Stockists",
          "selector": "html > body > main"
        },
        {
          "tag": "section",
          "role": null,
          "level": null,
          "text": "How we work Manuscripts arrive by post. We read them away from a screen, answer every one, and take on two a year. An accepted book is edited over eight months, set in metal for the title pages, and printed in runs of nine hundred. Nothing is reprinted. When a run is gone the book stays gone, which keeps the shelf honest and the workshop quiet.",
